I left out both operations-team requests. The node has no filesystem capability, since the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI, so it cannot write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. The metadata call would also send the subscription text to `metadata.internal.example`, which is not in the node's `HTTPClient` allowlist, so the host would trap the whole run. Logging and enrichment belong in the host or a node that declares those capabilities.

The node below pre-checks each URL against the four allowed hosts, so an out-of-scope subscription is recorded as a failure instead of trapping the run.

